1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,350
In 1990, Ireland's economy was 49 billion dollars. Sweden's was 261 billion.

2
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:10,150
Watch.

3
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:24,395
2025. Ireland: 722 billion. Sweden: 669. On paper, Ireland is bigger,

4
00:00:24,395 --> 00:00:27,875
with about half as many people.

5
00:00:28,275 --> 00:00:35,525
But a large part of Ireland's GDP is the profit of international companies that book their earnings there.

6
00:00:35,925 --> 00:00:40,851
That's why Ireland's own government uses a different measure for its budget.

7
00:00:40,851 --> 00:00:42,925
The full race is on our channel.
